 "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, -1)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3, -2)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,1)$ and $(3,-2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-2 - (1)}{3 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-3\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(0,-1)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (-1) &= -3(x - (0)) \\\\\ny - (-1) &= -3 x \\\\\ny &= -3 x -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487498 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f05d5dc-1f1f-5341-bed0-2a40038347de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 -\\frac{x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f05d5dc-1f1f-5341-bed0-2a40038347de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 -\\frac{x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487491} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9db8c26-61f5-5a2d-9290-3fd2495a2f22" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487504}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "845f9834-f22b-53bc-a424-04017a3a9353" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(3, 4)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(5, -2)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(5,-2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} 