(x - (-3)) \\\\\ny - (3) &= \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3b1e17e-b281-5dda-86ff-43b200f959e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3b1e17e-b281-5dda-86ff-43b200f959e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487510} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2d46d7-e9a5-5f5a-8dc6-05b51f351ec5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487508}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e690e28-5baa-55f2-888d-294c615d87b1" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(0, 4)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, 1)$ and $(3, -1)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,1)$ and $(3,-1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-1 - (1)}{3 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-2\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(0,4)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (4) &= -2(x - (0)) \\\\\ny - (4) &= -2 x \\\\\ny &= 4 -2 x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "629e4a61-587c-549d-96ab-2d80c984c89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 x -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "629e4a61-587c-549d-96ab-2d80c984c89d" :answer/type {:db/ide