sses through the point $(-3, 3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(5, 1)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(5,1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 - (-1)}{5 - (2)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(-3,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= \\frac{2}{3}(x - (-3)) \\\\\ny - (3) &= \\frac{2 x}{3} + 2 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2 x}{3} + 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0bcaabb-3c95-55ba-9dcf-7a35953d4082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0bcaabb-3c95-55ba-9dcf-7a35953d4082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 -x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487509} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74f997c-c7cd-5d70-89ae-414d8a64d72a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487513}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ebcde1e1-9558-5044-b7d6-26cd0859557b" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(1, 3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(2, -1)$ and $(4, -3)$.$y =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(2,-1)$ and $(4,-3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-3 - (-1)}{4 - (2)} \\\\\n&= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of\n\n$$\n-1\n$$\n\nand passes through the point $(1,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use the point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (3) &= -1(x - (1)) \\\\\ny - (3) &= 1 -x \\\\\ny &= 4 -x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line Passing Through Two Points"}]}
